## Files to know

- `mkdocs-api-ref.yml`  
  API reference site (auto-generated).

- `mkdocs.yml`  
  Main documentation site (Marimo-first tutorials and narrative docs).

- `docs_scripts/gen_ref_pages.py`  
  Top-level API reference generator/orchestrator. Discovers modules, writes generated pages/nav, and writes the API inventory.

- `docs_scripts/ref_introspect.py`  
  Source-analysis and runtime-introspection helpers used by the API generator. Collects module/class members, inheritance metadata, doc ownership, and property/member tables.

- `docs_scripts/ref_render.py`  
  Markdown rendering helpers for generated API pages. Emits module pages, class pages, member tables, mkdocstrings blocks, and inherited-render markers.

- `docs_scripts/api_hooks.py`  
  API-site HTML post-processing hook. Cleans marked mkdocstrings blocks, rewrites rendered `api:` links/citations, strips inherited base-render wrappers, and prunes redundant TOC entries.

- `docs_scripts/main_hooks.py`  
  Main-docs hook: rewrites `api:` links to point to `/reference/...` URLs. Hard-fails on missing/ambiguous targets.

- `docs_scripts/api_inventory.py`  
  Inventory format, progressive-qualification resolver, URL helpers, and shared Markdown `api:` link rewriting used by both hooks/build stages.

- `serve.py`  
  Builds both sites, merges them, and either serves locally or writes to `site/` with `--build-only`. It also cleans up the generated `docs/_api_inventory.json` file after builds.